  <subsection xml:id="unit1-project1-roadtrip">
    <title>Project 1: Road Trip Budget Planner</title>
   
    <p>A family is planning a road trip and wants to estimate fuel costs, food costs, and 
        see if they qualify for a random travel discount. You will write code to plan their road trip budget.
    </p>

  <p>Program Requirements: Ask the user for the following information and store the input into variables.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Driver's name</li>
    <li>Total trip miles</li>
    <li>Vehicle miles per gallon</li>
    <li>Gas price per gallon</li>
    <li>Number of travelers</li>
    <li>Food budget per person</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Calculate the following and store the results into variables:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Gallons of gas needed</li>
    <li>Fuel cost</li>
    <li>Total food cost</li>
    <li>Total trip cost</li>
    <li>Average cost per traveler</li>
    <li>Whole number of gas stops (assume there will be a stop every 120 miles)</li>
    <li>Remaining miles after the last full gas stop</li>
    <li>Random discount between 5% and 20% (divide by 100 to convert to decimal)</li>
    <li>Discounted total</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Display a formatted trip summary (see sample below).</p>
<pre>
Sample output:
---------------------------------
ROAD TRIP SUMMARY
—------------------------------
Driver: Maria
Number of Travelers: 4
Gas Needed: 30.18 gallons
Fuel Cost: $108.35
Food Cost: $220.00
Total Cost: $328.35
Average Cost Per Traveler: $82.09
Random Discount: 14%
Discounted Cost: $282.38
Estimated Gas Stops: 8
Miles After Last Stop: 45
</pre>


  <project label="unit1-project1-roadtrip">
  <statement>
    <p>Calculate a road trip budget from the inputs of driver name, total trip miles, vehicle miles 
        per gallon, gas price per gallon, number of travelers, and food budget per person. Calculate
        the gallons of gas needed, fuel cost, total food cost, total trip cost, average cost per traveler,
        whole number of gas stops, remaining miles after the last full gas stop, random discount,
        and discounted total. Display a formatted trip summary like below.
        Please use the variables provided in the starting code below.
        Run your code at least once with the following input for autograding: 
        <pre>
Sample input: Pat, 200, 30, 4.00, 3, 15
---------------------------------
ROAD TRIP SUMMARY
---------------------------------
Driver: Pat
Number of Travelers: 3
Gas Needed: 6.67 gallons
Fuel Cost: $26.67
Food Cost: $45.00
Total Cost: $71.67
Average Cost Per Traveler: $23.89
Random Discount: 13%
Discounted Cost: $62.35
Estimated Gas Stops: 1
Miles After Last Stop: 80.00
        </pre>
    </p>
</statement>
<program interactive="activecode" language="python">
<code>
import random

# 1. Input: get the following input from the user 
#    Convert the numerical inputs to float or int
driver = 
miles = 
mpg = 
gas_price = 
travelers = 
food_budget = 

# 2. Calculate the following
gallons_needed = 
fuel_cost = 
food_cost = 
total_cost = 
average_cost = 
gas_stops = 
remaining_miles = 

# 3. Generate a random discount from 5% to 20% using random.randint() 
#    Divide by 100 to convert to decimal
discount =

# 4. Calculate the discounted amount and total 
discount_amount = 
discounted_total = 

# 5. Print the results of all of calculations (see sample output above)
</code>
<tests>
from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui

class myTests(TestCaseGui):

    def findLine(self, lines, target):
        for line in lines:
            if "#" in line:
                index = line.find("#")
                line = line[0:index]
            if target.replace(" ", "") in line.replace(" ", ""):
                #print(line)
                return line
        return "None"
            
    def run_file(self, code, inputs):
        print("****************************************************************************")
        print("Testing code with inputs: " + inputs)
        print("****************************************************************************")

        lines = code.split("\n")
        ins = inputs.split(",")
        inN = 0

        for i in range(len(lines)):
            if "input" in lines[i] and not "#" in lines[i]:
                equals = lines[i].find("=") + 1
                lines[i] = lines[i][0:equals] + ins[inN]
                inN += 1

        code = "\n".join(lines)
        
        # Create an isolated scope for the code execution
        scope = {}
        exec(code, scope)
        
        # print(scope)
        return scope

    def testOne(self):
        code = self.getEditorText()

        lines = code.replace(" ", "").split("\n")

        line1 = self.findLine(lines,"gallons_needed") 
        self.assertIn("miles/mpg", line1, "gallons_needed can be calculated using miles, mpg, and /")

        line2 = self.findLine(lines,"fuel_cost")
        self.assertIn("gallons_needed*gas_price",line2,"fuel_cost can be calculated using gallons_needed, gas_price, and *.")

        line3 = self.findLine(lines,"food_cost")
        self.assertIn("travelers*food_budget",line3,"food_cost can be calculated using travelers, food_budget, and *.")

        line4 = self.findLine(lines,"average_cost")
        self.assertIn("total_cost/travelers",line4,"average_cost can be calculated using total_cost, travelers, and /.")

        line5 = self.findLine(lines,"gas_stops")
        self.assertIn("miles//120",line5,"gas_stops can be calculated using miles, 120, and //.")

        line6 = self.findLine(lines,"remaining_miles")
        self.assertIn("miles%120",line6,"remaining_miles can be calculated using miles, 120, and %.")

        line7 = self.findLine(lines,"random.randint")
        self.assertIn("random.randint(5,20)",line7,"discount can be generated using random.randint(5, 20).")
    
        line8 = self.findLine(lines,"discounted_total")
        self.assertIn("total_cost-discount_amount",line8,"discounted_total can be calculated using total_cost and discount_amount.")

        output = self.run_file(code, "\"Pat\", 200, 30, 4.00, 3, 15")
        output = self.findLine(str(output).split(","), "average_cost")
        self.assertIn("23.8", output, "average_cost starts with 23.8 if you enter the test case input: Pat, 200, 30, 4.00, 3, 15")

        output2 = self.run_file(code, "\"Pat\", 500, 25, 3.50, 2, 10")
        output2 = self.findLine(str(output2).split(","), "average_cost")
        self.assertIn("45.0", output2, "average_cost starts with 45.0 if you enter the test case input: Pat, 500, 25, 3.50, 2, 10")

        self.assertNotIn("23.8", code, "23.8 should not be hard-coded in the code")  
     

myTests().main()
</tests>
</program>
</project>

