<subsection>
    <title>Unit 1 Coding Project 2: Event Invitation Generator</title>



<p>A community center is hosting its annual Community Fun Run and wants a program 
    that automatically creates personalized invitations and printable name badges for participants. 
    The program should personalize the invitation using information entered by the user.
    </p>

 <p>Program Requirements: Ask the user for the following information and store the input into 
    variables.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>First Name</li>
        <li>Last Name</li>
        <li>Favorite Hobby</li>
        <li>Favorite Color</li>
        <li>City</li>
    </ul>

    <p>In your code, create the following:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>A full name using string concatenation.</li>
        <li>Initials using the first letter of the first and last names.</li>
        <li><p>A Badge ID using:
            <ul>
                <li>First 3 letters of the first name</li>
                <li>First 3 letters of the last name</li>
                <li>Random two-digit number</li>
            </ul>
            </p></li>
        <li><p>An Invitation Code using:
            <ul>
                <li>First 2 letters of the city</li>
                <li>First 2 letters of the hobby</li>
                <li>Random three-digit number</li>
            </ul>
            </p></li>
        <li>A Lucky Prize Number (1–100).</li>

    </ul>

<p>Display the personalized invitation and name badge (see sample below).</p>

<pre>
Sample output:
===================================
Community Fun Run Invitation
===================================
Hello Dani Garcia!
You are officially invited to the Community Fun Run
October 12 at 9:00 AM
Riverside Park
Please wear something blue and be prepared
to share your favorite hobby: painting!
Invitation Code: Chpa428
Lucky Prize Number: 57
----------------------------------
NAME BADGE
----------------------------------
COMMUNITY FUN RUN
Name: Dani Garcia
Initials: DG
City: Chicago
Badge ID: DanGar84
----------------------------------
We look forward to seeing you!
</pre>


<project label="unit1-project2-invitation">
  <statement>
    <p>Create a personalized invitation and name badge from the inputs of  
        first name, last name, favorite hobby, favorite color, and city. 
        Create the full name, initials, badge id, invitation code, and lucky number.
        Display a formatted invitation and name badge like below.
        Use the variables provided in the starting code below. Run it at least once 
        with the following input for auto-grading:
        <pre>
Input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago

Sample output:
===================================
Community Fun Run Invitation
===================================
Hello Dani Garcia!
You are officially invited to the Community Fun Run
October 12 at 9:00 AM
Riverside Park
Please wear something blue and be prepared
to share your favorite hobby: painting!
Invitation Code: Chpa428
Lucky Prize Number: 57
----------------------------------
NAME BADGE
----------------------------------
COMMUNITY FUN RUN
Name: Dani Garcia
Initials: DG
City: Chicago
Badge ID: DanGar84
----------------------------------
We look forward to seeing you!
</pre>
    </p>
    </statement>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python">
        <code>
import random

# 1. Input: get the following input from the user 
first_name =
last_name =
favorite_hobby =
favorite_color =
city =

# 2. Create the full name of the participant
full_name =

# 3. Get the initials (first letter of first name and first letter of last name)
initials =

# 4. Create the badge id for the participant
#    Use the first three letters of the first name, the first three letters of the last name, 
#    and a random two-digit number
badge_id =

# 5. Create the invitation code for the participant
#   Use the first two letters of the city, the first two letters of the hobby, 
#   and a random three-digit number
invitation_code =

# 6. Calculate a random lucky number for the participant from 1 - 100
lucky_number =
# print out the invitation and the name badge using the sample output above as a guide

</code>
<tests>
from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui

class myTests(TestCaseGui):
    def findLine(self, lines, target):
        for line in lines:
            if "#" in line:
                index = line.find("#")
                line = line[0:index]
            if target.replace(" ", "") in line.replace(" ", ""):
                #print(line)
                return line
        return "None"
            
    def run_file(self, code, inputs):
        print("****************************************************************************")
        print("Testing code with inputs: " + inputs)
        print("****************************************************************************")

        lines = code.split("\n")
        ins = inputs.split(",")
        inN = 0

        for i in range(len(lines)):
            if "input" in lines[i] and not "#" in lines[i]:
                equals = lines[i].find("=") + 1
                lines[i] = lines[i][0:equals] + ins[inN]
                inN += 1

        code = "\n".join(lines)
        
        # Create an isolated scope for the code execution
        scope = {}
        exec(code, scope)
        
        # print(scope)
        return scope
    
    def testOne(self):
        code = self.getEditorText()
        lines = code.split("\n")

        line = self.findLine(lines, "full_name=")
        self.assertTrue(("first_name" in line) and ("last_name" in line) and ('" "' in line), 'full_name should combine first_name, a space (" "), and last_name.')

        line = self.findLine(lines,"initials=")
        self.assertIn("first_name[0]", line, "first_name[0] gets the first letter of first_name for the initials")

        line = self.findLine(lines,"badge_id=")
        self.assertIn("first_name[0:3]",line,"first_name[0:3] gets the first 3 letters of first_name.")

        line = self.findLine(lines,"random.randint(")
        self.assertIn("random.randint(10",line,"random.randint used starting at 10 for a 2-digit number")

        line = self.findLine(lines,"invitation_code=")
        self.assertIn("city[0:2]",line,"city[0:2] gets the first two letters of the city.")

        output = self.run_file(code, "\"Dani\", \"Garcia\", \"painting\", \"blue\", \"Chicago\"")
        line = self.findLine(str(output).split(","), "favorite_color")
        self.assertIn("blue", line, "favorite_color should be printed in the invitation.")

        line = self.findLine(str(output).split(","), "badge_id")
        self.assertIn("DanGar", line, "Badge ID should start with DanGar for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")

        line = self.findLine(str(output).split(","), "invitation_code")
        self.assertIn("Chpa", line, "Invitation Code should start with Chpa for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")

        line = self.findLine(str(output).split(","), "full_name")
        self.assertIn("Dani Garcia", line, "Full name should be printed in the invitation for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")

        self.assertNotIn("Dani Garcia", code, "Dani Garcia should not be hard-coded in the code")

myTests().main()
</tests>
</program>
</project>

